{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1772133,"ns":0,"title":"(B, N) pair","extract":"In mathematics, a (B, N) pair is a structure on groups of Lie type that allows one to give uniform proofs of many results, instead of giving a large number of case-by-case proofs. Roughly speaking, it shows that all such groups are similar to the general linear group over a field.","description":"Concept in group theory","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}